1110675001-941b9057-b966-445a-847d-30ff31fdebf7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c3da18f8d54aff595f5ecc990d890f225596f545253b82562d0557a4365812f7","event_uuid":"5c2c9240-4f8b-499e-ab75-9691bf155c00","position":{"commit_sha":"23eb57f41d06c131aed3349b838a5224afbfdba1","position":"1785621791591024001-5c2c9240-4f8b-499e-ab75-9691bf155c00"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"50f528e73261ce68f2704f6eabf1795d8126cbedddf77f406aa17c39620e0964","event_uuid":"081c4066-01a6-454b-b0dd-0af52c04c220","position":{"commit_sha":"ced1ca88ba18e1d2e761480c5556329a5cf47bf2","position":"1785622289385131001-081c4066-01a6-454b-b0dd-0af52c04c220"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"374eb9142a2cfc86264f9e7e566fb343c2cf543600543816b9d4c7d771c6f3e6","event_uuid":"c7a37e72-1d02-4ad6-868c-9fc9d46616c9","position":{"commit_sha":"df24fa2a3d131022c487234a7368a07afca98385","position":"1785622302031126001-c7a37e72-1d02-4ad6-868c-9fc9d46616c9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD evidence: all 5 final oracle nodes were observed RED before production edits. A separate standard-tier implementer saw only the primary test and completed in one attempt. Restored edge/E2E/doc tests pass; focused caused_by suite is 14/14 green; exact acceptance selectors  and  pass; lint/typecheck pass. Mutation treating failed blame as successful-empty made both partial-failure unit and real close-path tests fail, proving the guard prevents an incorrect persisted caused_by link.","timestamp":1785622289385131001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to prior shell-mangled selectors: all 5 final oracle nodes were observed RED before production edits. A separate standard-tier implementer saw only the primary test and completed in one attempt. Restored edge, close-path, and doc tests pass; focused caused_by suite is 14 of 14 green; exact acceptance selectors in tests/unit/metrics/test_blame.py for distinguishes and partial_failure pass; lint and typecheck pass. Mutation treating failed blame as successful-empty made both partial-failure unit and real close-path tests fail, proving the guard prevents an incorrect persisted caused_by link.","timestamp":1785622302031126001}],"created_at":1785372546159906001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"Document how to clone this repo cheaply, state the one accepted degradation honestly, and fix the\nlatent wrong-answer bug that degradation would otherwise cause. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Doc\nRecord `--filter=blob:none` guidance with the measured numbers (full **1.04 GiB / 59 s** vs blobless\n**68.7 MiB / 14.3 s**), and that `--filter=tree:0` must never be used here (measured **3.57 GiB**,\n3.4x larger than full). Note that rebar itself cannot filter a clone it does not perform.\n\n## The code fix (why it belongs with the doc)\n`git blame` over historical trees runs on a real rebar path: `metrics/blame.py:69` <-\n`_blame_file_commits` <- `derive_caused_by` (`:94`) <- `transition_close.py:514`, i.e. **on every bug\nclose without an explicit `--caused-by`**. Under a blobless promisor this faults blobs one at a time.\n\n**Prerequisite the earlier draft missed (plan-review G6 remediation): failure and emptiness are\ncurrently indistinguishable.** `_blame_file_commits` (`blame.py:67-79`) returns `[]` BOTH when the\ngit call fails (`if out is None: return []`) AND when a successful blame yields no SHAs. So\n\"abort on any per-path failure\" is **not implementable as stated** — there is nothing to detect.\nThis ticket must therefore FIRST change `_blame_file_commits` to return `None` on git failure and\n`[]` on a successful-but-empty result, and only then have `derive_caused_by` abort on `None`.\nTreating a legitimately empty file as a failure would suppress correct derivations.\n\nTotal failure is benign (`blame.py:37` returns `None`). **Partial failure is not:**\n`derive_caused_by` loops per path and tallies across all of them, so if blame succeeds on some paths\nand fails on others — entirely plausible with a partly-warm object store — the strict-majority test\nruns over a **subset** and can elect a culprit that would not have won over the full set. That writes\na **wrong `caused_by` link**, which is worse than writing none.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `_blame_file_commits` returns **`None`** on git failure and **`[]`** on a successful-but-empty\n      blame — the two are distinguishable. Tier: **unit** with both fixtures.\n      Proving command: `pytest tests/unit/metrics/test_blame.py -k distinguishes -v`.\n- [ ] `derive_caused_by` returns `None` when `_blame_file_commits` returns `None` for **any** path,\n      rather than tallying a partial set. Tier: **unit** injecting a per-path git failure.\n      Proving command: `pytest tests/unit/metrics/test_blame.py -k partial_failure -v`.\n- [ ] A path whose blame legitimately yields **zero** lines does **not** abort the derivation (the\n      negative control that keeps correct derivations working). Tier: **unit**.\n- [ ] No `caused_by` link event is written in that case. Tier: **integration** on the close path\n      asserting the event set.\n- [ ] With all paths succeeding, the derived culprit is unchanged from today — the negative control.\n      Tier: **unit** golden comparison.\n- [ ] The guidance doc exists, states the measured numbers, names the accepted `git blame`\n      degradation, and is linked from the docs index. Tier: **doc-existence + content check**.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/metrics/blame.py`, `docs/` guidance page, tests\n\nScope: S. No dependencies.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/blame.py","reason":"abort on any per-path failure"},{"path":"docs/","reason":"clone guidance page"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc","parent_status_uuid":"941b9057-b966-445a-847d-30ff31fdebf7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"42fa-676d-fbbb-4ac5","ticket_type":"story","title":"B4: clone-guidance doc + make derive_caused_by abort on any per-path blame failure","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3b155daf-4d59-422b-a22e-7a344115d600","6932ddce-1b0f-4b10-b130-1591f5858f87","aaa18242-a2ba-4cfa-b984-410dfb29439c","098b4aa9-e306-48a0-a342-280b144dea41","941b9057-b966-445a-847d-30ff31fdebf7","5c2c9240-4f8b-499e-ab75-9691bf155c00","081c4066-01a6-454b-b0dd-0af52c04c220","c7a37e72-1d02-4ad6-868c-9fc9d46616c9"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785622302031126002,"uuid":"eb5d843c-15d3-4260-b446-37875d2320cc"}